<title>USA: Medi-Ject gets Norwegian reimbursement.</title>
<headline>Medi-Ject gets Norwegian reimbursement.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Medi-Ject Corp said Tuesday that it received approval for reimbursement from the Norwegian Health Ministry.</p>
<p>The Medi-Jector, a system for delivering insulin without using a needle, will be made available without charge to children under 16 years of age with diabetes. Norway's decision comes after four years of evaluation, it added.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
